  "description": {
    "text": "Battle Road Spring 2006 held nine tournaments in seven cities from 19 March to 30 April 2006, open to players drawn by lottery from those who applied by 17 February. Everyone in the qualifying round got Kouki Saitou's holofoil Deoxys δ, finalists the holo Stadium Battle Road Stadium, and the top three of each division the Victory Ring with Pikachu, in a plaque decorated with Groudon and Kyogre. The junior and senior winners went to the 2006 World Championships in the United States.",
